---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Pool from "../components/Pool.astro";
import Coverage from "../components/Coverage.astro";
const commands = {
 source: "git clone https://github.com/Ludion-ai/ludion.git\ncd ludion\nnpm ci\nnpm run build -w ludion-ai",
 scan: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js scan --dir /path/to/app",
 init: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js init --dir /path/to/app --ecosystem npm",
 patch: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js patch --dir /path/to/app",
 apply: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js patch --dir /path/to/app --apply",
 watch: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js watch --dir /path/to/app --apply --interval 900",
};
const config=JSON.stringify({schema:1,ecosystem:"npm",image:"node:24-slim",test:["npm","test"],timeout_seconds:120},null,2);
---
<Base title="Try the multi-stack preview | Ludion" description="Check PHP Docker, npm, Composer and Maven security updates. Choose an update policy and application test before applying source changes.">
 <article class="start-page wrap">
  <header class="page-intro"><h1>One workflow. More of your stack.</h1><p class="intro">Scan the project, choose an ecosystem policy, then validate its security update against your application.</p></header>
  <Pool>
   <section class="sync" aria-labelledby="scan">
    <div class="install"><h2 id="scan">Check your project</h2><p class="where">Source preview · Node 24+ · Docker for acquisition and validation. The published npm 0.1.4 release does not include these commands.</p><p>After building this source revision, run:</p><div class="command primary-command"><pre><code id="scan-command">{commands.scan}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="scan-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy scan command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p class="wiring">Replace /path/to/app with your project directory. Scan detects supported lockfiles and the configured PHP Dockerfile. Maven resolves its graph in a manifest-only container. The original project is not modified.</p></div>
    <aside class="path" aria-labelledby="update-path"><h3 id="update-path" class="visually-hidden">The update path</h3><ol class="flow"><li><span class="step-title">Detect</span><span class="step-detail">Installed versions and relevant advisories</span></li><li><span class="step-title">Validate</span><span class="step-detail">Your application test, old and new</span></li><li><span class="step-title">Apply</span><span class="step-detail">Recorded source updates</span></li></ol></aside>
   </section>
   <p class="coverage">PHP Docker · npm · Composer · Maven. An unavailable database or unsupported inventory stays visible. Production is not automatically redeployed.</p>
   <section class="reference" aria-labelledby="setup-details"><h2 id="setup-details">From discovery to a validated update</h2>
    <details open><summary><span>1 · Build the source preview</span><span class="summary-note">Keep the existing npm install separate</span></summary><div class="detail-body"><p>Use the multi-stack source revision. These commands become available on the default branch when its pull request is merged.</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="source-command">{commands.source}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="source-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy source setup" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div></div></details>
    <details><summary><span>2 · Choose the ecosystem and test</span><span class="summary-note">Required before validation</span></summary><div class="detail-body"><p>Choose php, npm, composer or maven. A project may scan several ecosystems together; its saved patch policy selects one manager at a time.</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="init-command">{commands.init}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="init-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy init command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>Edit ludion.security.json to select an official tool image matching your application and its real offline test command. npm acquisition uses npm 12.2.1; its Node tool image must support that version.</p><div class="command"><pre><code>{config}</code></pre></div><p>Tests must run with a read-only project and write only to supported scratch areas. Maven's online model excludes custom build/plugin configuration; those plugins must already be available for offline tests or validation will stop.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><span>3 · Validate, then apply</span><span class="summary-note">Source changes are opt-in</span></summary><div class="detail-body"><p>Acquire dependencies separately, run baseline/candidate tests offline and recheck the candidate inventory:</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="patch-command">{commands.patch}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="patch-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy validation command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>To validate again and apply only on success:</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="apply-command">{commands.apply}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="apply-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy apply command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>Review .ludion/security/ for the receipt and recovery journal. npm/Composer may adjust dependency constraints within the same major and regenerate the lockfile. Maven can add dependencyManagement constraints for vulnerable transitives. Major-version fixes and unresolved cases require review. Deploy through your normal process.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><span>4 · Keep checking automatically</span><span class="summary-note">While the process is running</span></summary><div class="detail-body"><p>Repeat the saved ecosystem policy every 900 seconds:</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="watch-command">{commands.watch}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="watch-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy watch command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>Ctrl+C requests a stop. An in-flight Docker step may finish, but a pending update will not be applied after cancellation is received. A partially interrupted multi-file change blocks further updates until its journal is recovered.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><span>What leaves your machine</span><span class="summary-note">Requests and boundaries</span></summary><div class="detail-body privacy"><p>Package names and exact versions are sent to OSV. PHP uses php.net metadata. Tool images and dependencies come from the configured public sources; Composer ZIP redirects are checked before every request. npm URL/Git/file sources are disabled and Maven repositories are mirrored to public Central.</p><p>Application source is sent to your configured Docker daemon for offline tests; choose a local daemon to keep it on your machine. No source is uploaded to Ludion and security commands send no telemetry. Online acquisition contains manifests only. Source snapshots exclude .env files, Git history and common credential directories, but they are not general secret scanners. This website uses Google Analytics; legacy sync request counting is unchanged.</p></div></details>
    <p class="privacy-summary">Known advisories and recorded application tests only. No match is not a security guarantee. Supported scope and unhandled cases stay explicit.</p>
   </section>
  </Pool>
 </article>
 <Coverage />
</Base>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]").forEach((button) => {
    const code = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy!);
    if (!code) return;
    button.hidden = false;
    const label = button.textContent;
    let reset: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>;

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      clearTimeout(reset);
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent ?? "");
        button.textContent = button.dataset.copied ?? label;
      } catch {
        const range = document.createRange();
        range.selectNodeContents(code);
        const selection = window.getSelection();
        selection?.removeAllRanges();
        selection?.addRange(range);
        button.textContent = button.dataset.selected ?? label;
      }
      reset = setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = label; }, 2000);
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .start-page {
    max-width: calc(1040px + var(--gutter) * 2);
  }
  .page-intro {
    padding-block: 16px 64px;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-title, clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px));
    font-weight: 560;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    max-width: 35em;
    font-size: var(--font-body, 16px);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .sync {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 15rem;
    gap: 48px 80px;
    padding-top: 48px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 560;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .where {
    margin: 12px 0 24px;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .command {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 16px;
  }
  .primary-command {
    padding: 22px;
  }
  pre {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  pre code {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .primary-command pre code {
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  button {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    min-height: 40px;
    min-width: 48px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 4px 6px;
    margin: -2px -4px 0 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  button:hover {
    background: var(--paper-2);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  button[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .result {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .result code {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .wiring {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    max-width: 42em;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .path {
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .flow {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .flow li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 36px 24px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .flow li:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-left-color: transparent;
  }
  .flow li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 5px;
    left: -4px;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--muted);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .step-title,
  .step-detail {
    display: block;
  }
  .step-title {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .step-detail {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .step-detail.file {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 12px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .coverage {
    margin: 36px 0 0;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .coverage a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 4px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .reference {
    margin-top: 72px;
  }
  .reference > h2 {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  details:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  summary {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px 24px;
    padding: 22px 28px 22px 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  summary::after {
    content: "+";
    position: absolute;
    right: 1px;
    top: 20px;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  details[open] > summary::after {
    content: "−";
  }
  summary:hover > :first-child {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .summary-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .detail-body {
    max-width: 44rem;
    padding-bottom: 28px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .detail-body > p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .detail-body .command + .command-label {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .detail-body .command-label {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .detail-body .consent {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .privacy-summary {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .sync {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 36px;
    }
    .flow {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 20px;
    }
    .flow li {
      padding: 18px 0 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .flow li::before {
      top: -4px;
      left: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .page-intro {
      padding-block: 8px 40px;
    }
    .sync {
      padding-top: 32px;
    }
    .primary-command {
      padding: 16px;
      gap: 8px;
    }
    .primary-command pre code {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .flow {
      grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);
      gap:0;
    }
    .flow li {
      padding:0 0 24px 20px;
      border-top:0;
      border-left:1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .flow li:last-child {padding-bottom:0;}
    .flow li::before {top:5px;left:-4px;}
    .step-title {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .step-detail {
      font-size: 12px;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .step-detail.file {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .reference {
      margin-top: 48px;
    }
    .summary-note {
      display: none;
    }
    .command {
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 14px;
    }
    .command pre code {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
